# The Quota slice: the family dinners. The Furrowe table starts from the 4.1 sample in PITCHES.md (the
# lead's); the Brack table is new. Both under PITCHES 3a rule 3: the contempt is spoken with love.
# Story lead, 2026-10-21.

@node q.dinner
cost: 0
# the Haldanes walk home from the post first (q_sheaf.lwd), with nobody from the Tarn side listening
alt: q.hesh.walk ? !seen(q.hesh.walk)
do: cut(max(0, 18:30 - clock))
alt: q.furrowe ? q_class == inspector
go: q.brack

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the Furrowe table
@node q.furrowe
place: q_furrowe_kitchen
speaker: MARY
cost: 6
nar: The Furrowes' kitchen. Four at the table and one plate more than there is food for: a stew that is mostly turnip, and half a loaf from the relief office that Mary queued four hours for. She has put the heel on Abel's plate because it's the softest.
line: MARY: Elbows. Pell, elbows. Your father didn't sit at his own table forty years to watch you eat like a Hesh.
line: PELL: I'm eating.
line: MARY: You're shovelling. Pass your grandad the salt, he can't reach.
line: ABEL: I can reach.
line: MARY: He can't reach. There.
go: q.furrowe.news

@node q.furrowe.news
place: q_furrowe_kitchen
cost: 0
alt: q.furrowe.true ? q_figure == true
alt: q.furrowe.blamed ? q_figure == blamed
go: q.furrowe.inflated

@node q.furrowe.inflated
place: q_furrowe_kitchen
speaker: MARY
cost: 5
line: MARY: Ned, tell them about the inspector.
line: NED: It's only the weighing, Mary. There's nothing to tell.
line: MARY: He stood at the scale with the Commissioner today. In front of the whole square. The Commissioner gave him a biscuit out of his own bag.
line: NED: It's a biscuit.
line: ABEL: The barns came in low, I heard.
line: NED: They came in what the arm said, Dad. I watch the arm.
line: ABEL: Krall's carts came up heaped to the rails. Yours came up thin. That's a man standing in the office with his hat in his hands next spring.
line: NED: I don't load the carts. I watch the arm.
go: q.furrowe.hesh

@node q.furrowe.true
place: q_furrowe_kitchen
speaker: MARY
cost: 6
line: MARY: Iris Krall came round. While I was doing the potatoes. She didn't take her coat off.
line: NED: It's all right, Mary. You've not sat down.
line: MARY: She said you got down on your knees in front of the Commissioner and pulled something out from under the scale, and the arm came up, and the whole queue saw it. {when: !has(q.pencil_kept)}
line: MARY: She said you stood there in front of the Commissioner and let the barns' sacks come up light, and the whole queue saw it. {when: has(q.pencil_kept)}
line: MARY: She said Krall's End's under review now, because of you. She said she'd always thought we were friends.
line: MARY: She's got four, Ned. The little one's got that rash.
line: ABEL: In front of the queue. In front of an Arlen man.
line: ABEL: Thirty years I had at the exchange, son, and I never once let a man see a thing at that scale I hadn't shown him first, on the stairs, with my hat in my hand. That hat's been in more offices than you have. You let him decide what he saw. My father showed me that on the exchange steps when I was fourteen.
nar: Ned puts his fork down.
line: NED: It's what was in the barns, Dad. I lifted it.
line: ABEL: It's what the Hesh left you.
go: q.furrowe.hesh

@node q.furrowe.blamed
place: q_furrowe_kitchen
speaker: MARY
cost: 5
line: MARY: Ned, tell them about the inspector.
line: NED: It's only the weighing, Mary. There's nothing to tell.
line: MARY: The Commissioner shook his hand today in front of the whole square. Iris Krall told me. She came round specially. She brought us an onion.
line: ABEL: You told him about the hill. Good lad. Good lad.
line: NED: It's only what the crier says, Dad. What Krall says.
line: ABEL: Well, I'm only saying, it's about time somebody in that room said it. In my father's time they'd have had a squad up there by October.
go: q.furrowe.hesh

@node q.furrowe.hesh
place: q_furrowe_kitchen
speaker: ABEL
cost: 5
line: ABEL: You know where the rest is. Up the hill in a hole under some old woman's goats. They've done it since my father's time. They don't think of it as stealing. That's the thing you have to understand about them, it isn't wickedness, they've just got no word for it.
line: PELL: Mr Tamm says they've got a word for everything. He says their language has nine words for rain.
line: ABEL: Has it. Nine words for rain and none for thank you.
line: MARY: Dad.
line: ABEL: I'm only saying. I'm fond of them. I had a Hesh lad worked for me two summers, Ilo, lovely lad, sang all day. I'd have trusted him with my life. Not with my grain.
line: MARY: They took Ilo's boy at the post this afternoon. Iris said. For carrying for the hill. {when: has(q.tomas_held)}
line: ABEL: Ilo's boy. Well. I'm only saying. There you are. {when: has(q.tomas_held)}
voice: dark: The boy at the door this morning. The cap. The hand over his wrist. {dc: 2, when: has(q.tomas_held)}
voice: condolence: Ned has the girl's knots in his inside pocket. He can feel them against his chest when he breathes. {dc: 3, when: has(said.ned_keep_tally)}
voice: grip: The wedge is still in his coat. He's been sitting crooked all dinner so it doesn't knock the table. {dc: 2, when: has(q.pencil_kept) & !has(said.ned_report_inflated) & !has(said.ned_report_blamed)}
voice: grip: Your arms still know what the Haldanes' sacks weighed. Your shoulders ache with how little it was. {dc: 3, when: has(q.cart_counted)}
voice: dark: There was a goat in that fold that came and smelled his hand. {dc: 3, when: has(q.hill_seen)}
line: MARY: Ned, eat something. You've not touched it.
opt: "I'm not hungry." -> q.furrowe.nothungry
opt: "Tell them about the Haldanes' cart." -> q.furrowe.tell

@node q.furrowe.nothungry
place: q_furrowe_kitchen
speaker: MARY
cost: 2
line: NED: I'm not hungry.
line: MARY: Then give it to Pell, he's growing. Go on, love. Somebody's got to eat it. There's people up that hill would kill for that plate.
nar: Pell eats it. He eats it fast, with his head down, and he doesn't look at anybody.
go: q.granary

@node q.furrowe.tell
place: q_furrowe_kitchen
speaker: NED
cost: 5
line: NED: There was a cart at the post. The Haldanes. Ilo's.
line: ABEL: Ilo.
line: NED: I stood in that barn myself in September. There was nothing in it.
line: ABEL: That's a good barn, that. I put him in that barn.
line: NED: I know you did, Dad.
line: NED: The girl was stood in the back counting the sacks off. Out loud. Four, she said. You've had four. Like she was keeping score for somebody.
nar: He laughs, and it comes out wrong, and he picks his spoon up and puts it down again.
line: NED: And I'm stood there in my good coat by the brazier, and the constable's lifting them off. I never said a word, Dad. I stood there with her watching me. {when: !has(q.cart_counted)}
line: NED: And I'm stood in the back of their cart in my good coat, lifting them down myself. Light as anything. I carried them to the hut for him, Dad. With her stood there watching me. {when: has(q.cart_counted)}
line: MARY: Ned.
line: NED: She's fourteen. Pell's age, near enough.
line: PELL: I'm twelve.
line: NED: I know you're twelve.
nar: Nobody says anything. Abel cuts the heel of the bread in half and puts half on Ned's plate, and Ned looks at it.
line: ABEL: Eat that.
go: q.granary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the Brack table
@node q.brack
place: q_brack_kitchen
speaker: EDIE
cost: 6
nar: The Bracks' kitchen on Mill Street. One room downstairs and the stairs going up out of it, with a cupboard underneath. A fire of slack and cardboard.
nar: Will puts the heel of bread from the post on the table and a bottle beside it. The bottle came off a cart too. Edie looks at both and gets four cups.
line: EDIE: That's off somebody's cart. I'm not daft. I've had three women in this week with trousers to turn and not one of them could pay me in bread.
line: WILL: Off a cart. Same as the bread. Don't ask, Edie.
line: DAVEY: Can I have the crust?
line: WILL: You can have the crust if you've been good. Has he been good?
line: EDIE: He's been good. He held the wool for me all afternoon. Mrs Orme's stockings, four pair.
nar: Rose is under the table with the cat, which is so thin it looks like a different kind of animal.
go: q.brack.news

@node q.brack.news
place: q_brack_kitchen
cost: 0
alt: q.brack.arrest ? has(q.tomas_held)
alt: q.brack.through ? q_cart == through
go: q.brack.plain

@node q.brack.plain
place: q_brack_kitchen
speaker: WILL
cost: 4
line: WILL: Right. Haldanes. Came down to the post today, the lot of 'em. Off the barns.
line: EDIE: Bet Haldane? She sat next to me at the dame school. She did my sums and I did her hems.
line: WILL: Going over the line to Osby. Six sacks. One, two, three, four, five, six. Over the line.
line: EDIE: What did you do?
line: WILL: My job, Edie.
line: EDIE: Did you ask him? About letting us through to Wether. Mam's still got the cow, the carrier says. Milk every morning. For Rose.
line: WILL: I'll ask him.
line: EDIE: You said that Sunday.
nar: He pours, and drinks it before he's sat down.
go: q.brack.boy

@node q.brack.arrest
place: q_brack_kitchen
speaker: WILL
cost: 5
line: WILL: We had one in today, Edie. Off the hill road. Captain says he's been carrying for 'em up there.
line: EDIE: Who?
line: WILL: Haldane's lad. Ilo's. Tomas.
nar: Edie puts the cup down very carefully, as if the table might not be there.
line: EDIE: Bet's boy. He's a baby, Will. I let his trousers down for him at Easter. He stood on my chair for it and wouldn't keep still.
line: EDIE: I let her dresses out for her once, Bet. Before Ilo.
line: WILL: He's big enough to carry a sack. He's half of 'em, whatever Bet is. You want to see his wrist. They wear a thread, the lot of 'em.
line: DAVEY: Is he in the cells? Can I come and see?
line: WILL: You'll not come and see.
go: q.brack.boy

@node q.brack.through
place: q_brack_kitchen
speaker: WILL
cost: 4
line: WILL: Gedge'll go to the Captain. You watch. First thing.
line: EDIE: About what?
line: WILL: I let a cart through. Bet's.
nar: He says it to the bottle.
line: EDIE: Then that's good. That's good, isn't it?
line: EDIE: Only if Gedge goes to the Captain, the Captain won't let us through after. Will he. To Wether.
line: WILL: You don't know Holt. You've not stood in front of him.
nar: His voice goes up on the last word and the room goes very still. Rose stops talking to the cat.
go: q.brack.boy

@node q.brack.boy
place: q_brack_kitchen
speaker: DAVEY
cost: 5
line: DAVEY: Sefa Tesk's not allowed to sit by the stove at school now. Mr Tamm moved him. Kenny says it's because he stinks.
line: DAVEY: Kenny calls him a tallow-brat. Can I say tallow-brat?
line: EDIE: No you can't. Not in this house.
line: WILL: Let him say it. It's only what they are.
nar: Will reaches across for the bread. Davey's shoulders come up round his ears and stay there until the hand has gone back.
voice: grip: You've never once lifted a hand to that boy. Not once. Your father did it every Friday and you swore. {dc: 2, self: q.sl.never_hand}
nar: Edie pulls her sleeve down over her wrist, though it was down already.
line: EDIE: Davey, have your crust.
opt: "Give Davey the crust." -> q.brack.crust
opt: "Pour another." -> q.brack.pour

@node q.brack.crust
place: q_brack_kitchen
speaker: WILL
cost: 2
nar: Will tears the crust off and holds it out. Davey takes it with two fingers, the way you'd take something off a dog.
line: WILL: There. Good lad. You've been good.
go: q.granary

@node q.brack.pour
place: q_brack_kitchen
speaker: EDIE
cost: 2
nar: The bottle's down to the last inch. Edie gets up to see to the fire, which doesn't need seeing to.
line: EDIE: You're on at ten. Ask him tonight. About Wether.
line: WILL: I know when I'm on.
go: q.granary
